  "worked_solution": "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $P$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=p+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nIn our case, the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=\u27e83,-2,5\u27e9.$\n\nUsing the formula for the vector equation of a line, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\u27e83,-2,5\u27e9+t\u27e84,1,6\u27e9,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
